            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Wholeness, flourishing, and the comprehensive restoration of relationships, specifically reconciliation between God and humanity and cosmic harmony, rooted in the Hebrew concept of shalom.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Isaiah 9:6\",\"John 14:27\",\"Romans 5:1\",\"Ephesians 2:14-17\",\"Colossians 1:20\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Inner tranquility and psychological rest or comfort in the midst of difficult circumstances.\",\"basis\":[\"Philippians 4:7\",\"John 16:33\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Socio-political harmony and the eschatological cessation of physical war or violence among nations.\",\"basis\":[\"Isaiah 2:4\",\"Micah 4:3\",\"Psalm 46:9\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The eternal rest and ultimate eschatological state of believers in the New Creation.\",\"basis\":[\"Revelation 21:1-4\",\"2 Peter 3:14\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"While colloquially understood in modern contexts as merely the absence of conflict, biblical scholarship overwhelmingly emphasizes peace (shalom in Hebrew, eirene in Greek) as a positive, dynamic state of holistic well-being, cosmic reconciliation, and right relationships inaugurated by Christ.\"}",
